<title>USA: San Francisco expects $24.5 mln budget surplus.</title>
<headline>San Francisco expects $24.5 mln budget surplus.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Francisco's budget should end the fiscal year in June with a $24.5 million surplus, according to a published report Friday.</p>
<p>San Francisco Chronicle reported that the budget has been buoyed by strong tax revenues. The strongest boost comes from the transfer tax on real estate sales. It is running $5.2 million ahead of expectations.</p>
<p>Similarly, hotel taxes are $3 million over projections, the Chronicle reported, citing a report by San Francisco's controller.</p>
